# folio.wasm (DESIGN §144): Folio's compiler as a WebAssembly module of its own. This program is it: compiler.folio
# reads a program, and wasm.folio makes it into the module folio build --target wasm makes. make-folio-wasm.mjs
# builds it into folio.wasm, by itself; the playground compiles with it.
#
# It's run with the program's text and the files it may use as its arguments: the text, then each file's name and
# text. It says one line: the module's bytes, each a number, with what running it needs in its section "folio"; or,
# for a mistake in the program, "mistake" and the mistake as JSON, its place and its reason.

use "wasm.folio" as webassembly

set folio_given to arguments
set folio_names to empty list
set folio_texts to empty list
set folio_k to 2
repeat while folio_k is less than length of folio_given
    add item folio_k of folio_given to folio_names
    add item (folio_k + 1) of folio_given to folio_texts
    set folio_k to folio_k + 2
end
try
    set folio_made to webassembly's wasm_compile(item 1 of folio_given, folio_names, folio_texts)
    say join webassembly's wasm_with_details(folio_made) with ","
if it fails with folio_why
    say "mistake " + (folio_why as json)
end
